=== A. IS lam_inf = 0 ADMISSIBLE?  (decay-to-zero families, fit 2 shape params to lr1,lr2) ===
  family lam=C exp(-c N^q), c>0,q>0 is a genuine decay to 0.
  F(q)=0 needed. F on q>0: [('0.001', '0.255476'), ('0.25', '0.312096'), ('0.5', '0.373035'), ('1', '0.508346'), ('2', '0.84168'), ('4', '1.85069')]
  F(q) > 0 for EVERY q>0 tested and increasing => NO ROOT with q>0.
  the only root is at q<0 (F(-2)=-0.08013, F(-1)=0.0639), and q<0 gives N^q->0 i.e. lam->C>0.
  family lam=C N^-p (pure power decay to 0): p from each consecutive pair = ['0.456018', '0.300174', '0.216884'] -> not constant, REFUTED
  => within the families tested, lam_inf > 0.  The SEQUENCE HAS A POSITIVE LIMIT is the part
     these four points DO determine; the VALUE is the part they do not.

=== B. MODEL-FREE INTERVAL (assumes only lam_min(N) non-increasing: Cauchy interlacing, nested basis) ===
